course: dictionary
lesson: 4678
title: Capital letters change meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and a capital letter can show which one is meant. With a capital H, the Holocaust means the murder of about six million Jewish people by the Nazis in Germany and lands they controlled during the Second World War. «The Nazis murdered about six million Jews, as well as many Roma, disabled people and others, only because of who they were; this is called the Holocaust.»
explain: With a small letter, holocaust means a huge destruction and killing, especially by fire or nuclear war. «A nuclear holocaust» is a terrible thing that people hope will never happen. Look at the clues: a capital letter often means a particular name or event.
explain: The word also has an old Bible meaning: a sacrifice that was completely burned. You will rarely meet this today, so you can skip it unless the text is about the Bible.
explain: Context helps you choose. Ask: is this text about history, or about a huge disaster? «We remember it so that such hatred never happens again» shows that the Holocaust is a history lesson about hatred, not just a word for something bad.
fact: The Holocaust, with a capital H, is the name of a specific event: the murder of about six million Jewish people by the Nazis in the Second World War.
fact: Holocaust Memorial Day remembers the victims of the Holocaust.
fact: The diary of Anne Frank tells one girl's story from this time.
fact: Lower case «holocaust» means a huge destruction and killing, such as «a nuclear holocaust».
fact: Learning about the Holocaust helps people remember the victims and stand against hatred, prejudice and bullying.
exercise: «The Nazis murdered about six million Jews, only because of who they were.» What does the Holocaust mean? | A famous painting | A very hot summer in Germany | A school trip to a museum | *The murder of about six million Jewish people by the Nazis in the Second World War
exercise: What does «a nuclear holocaust» mean? | *A huge destruction and killing, especially by nuclear war | A small fire in a kitchen | A sacrifice in a school play | A happy family party
exercise: Along with Jewish people, which other group did the Nazis murder? | *Roma | Teachers | Sailors | Farmers
test: «Holocaust Memorial Day» remembers whom? | *The victims of the Holocaust | Shopkeepers | Famous footballers | People who work with petrol
test: Which phrase uses the lower case meaning of holocaust? | Holocaust survivor | *a nuclear holocaust | Holocaust Memorial Day | remember the Holocaust
exam: Why do pupils learn about the Holocaust? | *So that people remember the victims and stand against hatred, prejudice and bullying | To learn how to cook | To practise their spelling
